   \[
   \text{If a person is young, then that person is rough.}
   \]  
   In relational terms, for any entity \(X\):  
   \[
   \text{Young}(X) \;\Rightarrow\; \text{Rough}(X)
   \]  
   There is **no “or”** in the policy, so it forms a **single group** with a single implicit condition (“the subject is young and therefore must be rough”).

2. **List the conditions implicit in the policy**  
